    "number": 375,
    "title": "Refresh the work guide for ADR 0007 and ADR 0008 and the stories filed on 2026-09-25",
    "body": "## Problem and resulting change\n\nThe committed guide dates from the 2026-09-25 06:57 UTC snapshot. Since then two decision records landed (ADR 0007, the B.U.N.N.Y. shell; ADR 0008, runtime hosting), the hub went from 116 to about 200 open stories, and H241, H37, N44, N113 and others closed. The Direction section still said the wall map grows into the shell, the topic texts described delivered work as pending, every topic's selections had closed so \"Useful next steps\" rendered empty, and the build refused the new stories for lack of roadmap nodes.\n\nThis is one intentional guide revision under #324, and the follow-up ADR 0007 and ADR 0008 named for the Direction text.\n\n- **Snapshot and history.** Backlog refreshed (202 open stories at the final refresh); `github-history.json` rebuilt with every previously recorded commit, PR and closed issue byte-identical.\n- **Roadmap and tracks.** 97 stories filed since the last refresh placed in new or existing nodes across new tracks (B.U.N.N.Y. shell, Hub moments, Now-playing follow-ups, Session settings, Producers, Monitor readability, Wall map retirement, LIFX Beam, Requested animations, Pixoo catalog, Delivery hygiene, Nanoleaf docs, Guide refresh, Guide navigation). Nodes whose work closed relabelled as delivered; `GUIDE_TRACKS` covers Adding devices and Engineering maintenance exactly; MILESTONES gains today's merges; cross edges added for N169 to the shell art and H44 to the Tronbyt transition.\n- **Direction.** BECOMING states ADR 0007 and ADR 0008 and adds moments and always-on; STANDING updated per surface; SEQUENCE keeps H20, H67, then H356, N169 with H355, H233 and the Nanoleaf wall presentation stories; DELIVERED_SINCE records H241, N44, N113 and H37.\n- **Topics.** All eleven action texts and selections rewritten against the snapshot and both ADRs; the hosting topic no longer says availability follows WSL until hosting moves off it.\n- **Evidence and text.** Completed-evidence rows corrected (Neon restyle, overview refresh, UI foundation, Panels trial, runtime availability, MCP media tools, LIFX) and twelve rows added for today's closures; the architecture intro and README track list updated.\n- **Refresh tooling.** The open-issue inventory is paginated (identical to #370, which this branch folds in; rebasing after #370 merges leaves only the status-reference change on that file); newly cited closed stories added to `GUIDE_STATUS_REFERENCES`.\n- **Tests and browser check made snapshot-aware.** `test_maintenance.py`: the blocker-injection fixture moves from the closed N111 to H356, and the Ideas test expects the snapshot's own idea marks beside its fixture picks. `check_guide.cjs`: H11 is now a snapshot idea, so the mock strips its saved highlight before adding the live one and the Ideas assertions are computed from the snapshot's marks; the roadmap tooltip expectation follows the relabel; the failed-repository badge check tolerates badges that leave with another repository's live-removed rows; the search summary pluralizes like the page.\n\nTracker writes made for this revision, recorded on the issues themselves: `next step` highlights on H356, H277, H355, N169, H233, N112, N81, N115, P79 and P76 (the Direction's next stories), a corrected idea reason on #271, Guide topics for thirteen stories other sessions filed without one, and heading or placement fixes on #342, #343, #358 and #360.\n\nNot changed: `architecture_diagrams.py` labels that still mention container hosting (#42) and retained Windows installations; re-rendering the viewers is a separate archify step. Blocked labels whose recorded blockers closed (H20, H201, H202, H254, H262, N90, N100, N110) are left for their owners.\n\nRefs #324. Follow-up of ADR 0007 (#271) and ADR 0008 (#44).\n\n## Scope and dependencies\n\nEvery changed path is under `docs/work-guide/`. No product, UI outside the guide, installation or device change. #370 is the standalone tooling PR for the pagination change; this branch carries the same code.\n\n## Validation\n\nFrom the worktree with Node 24 (`npm ci`):\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/refresh_backlogs.py`: exit 0 on the final run (earlier runs surfaced a live race with concurrently filed issues, which the paginated assertion now reports with its numbers).\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py`: exit 0; two consecutive builds produce identical HTML (SHA-256 `c8d7799b8215e5f4cb35bff9cf3775eeab0333a20563164ddc34b6a3d11c957c`). 11 guides, 202 primary open issues, 138 roadmap nodes, 9 diagrams.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py`: OK (56 tests).\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs`: exit 0 with Chromium 153.0.8010.12; screenshots and the receipt are retained outside Git.\n- `python3 docs/system-design/check.py`: pass (1,162 local links).\n- Retained in the main checkout's `.local/evidence/gh-324-guide-refresh/`: the HTML hash, the browser-check log, the maintenance-test log and the desktop screenshots.\n\n## Fixed comparison and reviews\n\n- Base `c851541` (main at branch creation; current main `21583cd` adds only the #354 test change outside the guide), head `3615588`, merge-base `c851541`.\n- `git diff c851541...3615588`, clean worktree.\n- Independent Standards and Specification reviews are recorded in comments against this comparison.\n- UI changes: guide only, under the SDLC guide-only UI approval exemption. Human approval for a UI candidate: not applicable.\n\n## Delivery\n\nGuide-only CI exception: both Depot workflows ignore `docs/work-guide/**`; the exception evidence (file list, trigger readback, zero check runs on the head and merge SHA, local checks) is recorded in a comment before the guarded squash merge. Public publication is a separate authorized step.\n\n## Work guide, when intentionally updated or published\n\nThis PR is the guide revision. Snapshot: final refresh on 2026-09-25 (see `snapshot.json` `refreshedAt`); source revisions per repository in `github-history.json` `headSha`; changed sections: Direction, all eleven topic guides, roadmap, history, completed evidence, Ideas; generated-output hash above; local checks above. Public edition not published by this PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
