    "number": 370,
    "title": "Paginate the open-issue inventory in the guide refresh",
    "body": "## Problem and resulting change\n\n`docs/work-guide/work/refresh_backlogs.py` reconciles the REST open-issue reads with one GraphQL query that reads the first 100 open issues per repository and asserts `hasNextPage` is false. The hub passed 100 open issues on 2026-09-25, so every refresh now fails with \"Paginate before accepting a larger inventory\" before it writes the snapshot. #324 and the nightly refresh (#315) both need the refresh to run.\n\nThe change reads each repository's open issues page by page with `after` cursors and merges them into one inventory whose `pageInfo` reports no next page, so `hub-native-deps.json` and `device-native-deps.json` keep the same shape for their consumers. The count assertion now includes its numbers, which made a live race with concurrently filed issues visible during the #324 refresh.\n\nRefs #324. Tooling only; no snapshot, generated output or guide text changes. The next guide revision (#324) folds this in by rebasing onto it.\n\n## Scope and dependencies\n\nOne file. No product, UI, installation or device change.\n\n## Validation\n\nFrom the worktree with Node 24:\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py` on the committed snapshot: exit 0, then `git diff --exit-code -- docs/work-guide/outputs`: no drift.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py`: OK.\n- `npm run check:workflow`: exit 0. `npm run test:workflow`: 15/15.\n- The patched refresh ran end to end in the #324 candidate worktree: hub inventory 123 open issues across two pages merged with `hasNextPage: false`, and the snapshot was written.\n\n## Fixed comparison and reviews\n\n- Base `21583cd` (main), head `1391f79`, merge-base `21583cd`.\n- `git diff 21583cd...1391f79`, clean worktree.\n- Independent Standards and Specification reviews are recorded in comments against this comparison.\n- UI changes: No. Human approval for a UI candidate: not applicable.\n\n## Delivery\n\nVerify all configured current-head PR jobs, guarded squash merge with `--match-head-commit`, and merged-revision main CI. #324 stays open for the guide revision.\n\n## Work guide, when intentionally updated or published\n\nNot updated by this PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
